st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X which sucks less.


Requirements
------------
In order to build st you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running st
----------
If you did not install st with make clean install, you must compile
the st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.

Fork customizations (wzj-zz/st-fork)
------------------------------------
This fork starts a tmux session automatically instead of a plain shell:

    tmux new-session -A -s main

- If ~/.tmux.conf exists, it is used as-is.
- Otherwise a builtin config is injected (mouse on, clipboard
  integration, and the keybindings below).

Builtin keybindings (Ctrl+Alt+...), active only without ~/.tmux.conf:

    C-M-c       new window
    C-M-n / C-M-p   next / previous window
    C-M-w       choose window (interactive list)
    C-M-, / C-M-.   swap window left / right (also C-M-u / C-M-o)
    C-M-v / C-M-s   split pane horizontally / vertically
    C-M-h/j/k/l select pane left / down / up / right
    C-M-[       zoom pane (toggle fullscreen)


